// A missing `{` for a function body must not fabricate a brace-less
// block that swallows the following declarations as its "body": the
// parser stops at the fault and synchronizes, so `let x = 5` is
// re-parsed as a top-level item instead of vanishing (audit §2.13).
// The expect wording was harmonized seed↔zig (audit §2.6), so the
// first line is byte-identical in both compilers.
// EXPECT-ERROR: expected '{' for function body, got let
fn f()
let x = 5
print(x)
